  "_comment": [
    "Actor scripts for the seven rendered cases (case_07 added 2026-09-15), transcribed from",
    "docs/dataset/scene-spec.md section 6. Positions are world metres; entities move",
    "by linear interpolation between waypoints, which is enough for 10 FPS at walking",
    "speed and keeps the ground truth exactly reproducible.",
    "",
    "'state' on a robot waypoint writes its telemetry channel. The ESTOP is read from",
    "this channel, never inferred from motion: a real robot reports its own stop, and",
    "inferring it from velocity would make the incident trigger depend on the tracker."
  ],
